  "tip1": "Break up sitting every 30 minutes – even a short walk helps your blood sugar and blood pressure.",
  "tip2": "WHO recommends 150–300 minutes of moderate activity per week for adults.",
  "tip3": "Change your position about every 15 minutes, even just shifting how you sit.",
  "tip4": "Place the top of your monitor at or slightly below eye level.",
  "tip5": "Take phone calls standing up – it’s free movement.",
  "tip6": "Keep a water bottle on your desk; every refill is a mini break.",
  "tip7": "Use the stairs and walk to a colleague instead of messaging.",
  "tip8": "Keep wrists straight while typing and let your elbows rest close to your body.",
  "exChinTuckName": "Chin Tuck",
  "exChinTuckSummary": "Undo “screen neck” by gliding your head straight back.",
  "exChinTuckSteps": "Sit tall with your feet flat and shoulders relaxed.\nKeep your eyes level and glide your chin and head straight back, making a gentle double chin.\nHold for 5 seconds, feeling a stretch at the base of the skull.\nRelease slowly and repeat.",
  "exChinTuckTip": "It is a small movement: don’t nod up or down.",
  "exNeckSideTiltName": "Neck Side Tilt",
  "exNeckSideTiltSummary": "Ease tension on the sides of the neck.",
  "exNeckSideTiltSteps": "Sit tall and let your shoulders drop away from your ears.\nSlowly tilt one ear toward the same-side shoulder, face looking forward.\nHold 15–30 seconds while breathing calmly.\nReturn to centre and repeat on the other side.",
  "exNeckSideTiltTip": "Don’t lift the shoulder to meet the ear and never bounce.",
  "exNeckRotationName": "Neck Rotation",
  "exNeckRotationSummary": "Restore the ability to look over your shoulder.",
  "exNeckRotationSteps": "Sit upright with shoulders down and look straight ahead.\nSlowly turn your head toward one shoulder as far as is comfortable, chin level.\nHold for 5 seconds.\nReturn to centre and turn to the other side.",
  "exNeckRotationTip": "Move slowly and keep your shoulders still.",
  "exLevatorStretchName": "Levator Scapulae Stretch",
  "exLevatorStretchSummary": "Target the stubborn knot between neck and shoulder blade.",
  "exLevatorStretchSteps": "Hold the edge of the seat with the hand of the side you want to stretch.\nTurn your head about 45° away from that side.\nLook down toward the opposite armpit.\nRest the other hand on the back of your head for light support and hold.",
  "exLevatorStretchTip": "Let the hand only rest on your head – don’t pull.",
  "exUpperTrapStretchName": "Upper Trapezius Stretch",
  "exUpperTrapStretchSummary": "Release the muscles that hold stress on your shoulders.",
  "exUpperTrapStretchSteps": "Hold the seat with the hand of the side to stretch to keep that shoulder down.\nTilt your ear toward the opposite shoulder, face forward.\nPlace the opposite hand on top of your head for gentle overpressure.\nHold 10–30 seconds and switch sides.",
  "exUpperTrapStretchTip": "Stop if you feel pain, tingling or numbness.",
  "exShoulderShrugsName": "Shoulder Shrugs",
  "exShoulderShrugsSummary": "Wake up tired upper shoulders in seconds.",
  "exShoulderShrugsSteps": "Sit tall with your arms hanging relaxed.\nLift both shoulders straight up toward your ears.\nPause for 1–2 seconds at the top.\nLet them drop fully and relax.",
  "exShoulderShrugsTip": "Lift straight up without rolling and keep your neck long.",
  "exShoulderRollsName": "Shoulder Rolls",
  "exShoulderRollsSummary": "Big, slow circles that loosen the whole shoulder girdle.",
  "exShoulderRollsSteps": "Sit tall with your arms relaxed.\nDraw large circles with your shoulders: up, back, down and forward.\nMake each circle slow and smooth.\nAfter half the reps, reverse the direction.",
  "exShoulderRollsTip": "Keep your head still and let only the shoulders move.",
  "exScapularSqueezeName": "Shoulder Blade Squeeze",
  "exScapularSqueezeSummary": "Counter rounded shoulders and activate your upper back.",
  "exScapularSqueezeSteps": "Sit upright, away from the backrest, elbows bent at your sides.\nDraw your shoulder blades back and together, slightly down.\nHold for 3–5 seconds with your chest open.\nRelease slowly.",
  "exScapularSqueezeTip": "Don’t shrug or arch your lower back.",
  "exCrossBodyStretchName": "Cross-Body Shoulder Stretch",
  "exCrossBodyStretchSummary": "Stretch the back of the shoulder after long mouse work.",
  "exCrossBodyStretchSteps": "Sit straight with your shoulders down.\nBring one straight arm across your chest at shoulder height.\nCup the elbow with your other hand and gently pull it toward you.\nHold 10–30 seconds and switch arms.",
  "exCrossBodyStretchTip": "Keep your torso facing forward – don’t rotate with the arm.",
  "exTricepsStretchName": "Overhead Triceps Stretch",
  "exTricepsStretchSummary": "Open the back of the arm and the side of the chest.",
  "exTricepsStretchSteps": "Raise one arm and bend the elbow so the hand drops behind your head.\nPoint the elbow to the ceiling, palm toward your upper back.\nWith the other hand, gently press the elbow back.\nHold about 20 seconds per arm.",
  "exTricepsStretchTip": "Keep your head upright; don’t push it forward.",
  "exChestOpenerName": "Seated Chest Opener",
  "exChestOpenerSummary": "Reverse the hunch: open the chest and front shoulders.",
  "exChestOpenerSteps": "Sit near the front of the seat and roll your shoulders down and back.\nInterlace your fingers behind you, palms facing your body.\nStraighten your arms and lift your hands gently until you feel a stretch.\nHold 10–30 seconds while breathing deeply.",
  "exChestOpenerTip": "Can’t clasp your hands? Hold your forearms or elbows instead.",
  "exThoracicExtensionName": "Thoracic Extension",
  "exThoracicExtensionSummary": "Bend the stiff upper back the other way over your backrest.",
  "exThoracicExtensionSteps": "Sit with feet flat and your mid-back against the top of the backrest.\nSupport your neck with your hands, elbows forward.\nLean back over the backrest, lifting your chest and looking up.\nHold 3–5 seconds and come back up slowly.",
  "exThoracicExtensionTip": "Move from the upper back, not the neck. Use a stable chair.",
  "exOverheadSideBendName": "Overhead Side Bend",
  "exOverheadSideBendSummary": "Lengthen the sides of your trunk and breathe deeper.",
  "exOverheadSideBendSteps": "Sit tall with both hips grounded on the seat.\nRaise your arms overhead and clasp your hands.\nBend slowly to one side from the waist.\nReturn to centre and bend to the other side.",
  "exOverheadSideBendTip": "Stay in one plane: don’t lean forward and keep both hips on the chair.",
  "exSpinalTwistName": "Seated Spinal Twist",
  "exSpinalTwistSummary": "Mobilise the spine and relieve a stiff back.",
  "exSpinalTwistSteps": "Sit upright, feet flat, arms crossed over your chest.\nKeep hips and knees facing forward.\nTurn your upper body to one side and hold for 5 seconds.\nReturn to centre and turn the other way.",
  "exSpinalTwistTip": "Grow tall before you twist and never force the end range.",
  "exCatCowName": "Seated Cat-Cow",
  "exCatCowSummary": "A flowing spine wave synced with your breath.",
  "exCatCowSteps": "Sit tall, feet flat, hands on your thighs.\nInhale (cow): arch your back, lift your chest and draw your shoulder blades together.\nExhale (cat): round your back, tuck your pelvis and bring your chin toward your chest.\nFlow slowly between the two.",
  "exCatCowTip": "Don’t jut your chin forward or drop your head back.",
  "exForwardFoldName": "Seated Forward Fold",
  "exForwardFoldSummary": "Let your back decompress and your mind slow down.",
  "exForwardFoldSteps": "Sit tall with your feet flat and apart.\nExhale and fold forward, resting your forearms on your thighs.\nLet your head, neck and spine form one long line.\nBreathe slowly, then roll up gradually.",
  "exForwardFoldTip": "Come up slowly – you may feel light-headed.",
  "exWristFlexorStretchName": "Wrist Flexor Stretch",
  "exWristFlexorStretchSummary": "Relieve forearms that type and click all day.",
  "exWristFlexorStretchSteps": "Extend one arm straight in front, palm facing up.\nWith the other hand, gently pull the fingers down toward the floor.\nKeep the elbow straight and hold 15–30 seconds.\nSwitch hands.",
  "exWristFlexorStretchTip": "Pull gently – you should feel a stretch, never pain.",
  "exWristExtensorStretchName": "Wrist Extensor Stretch",
  "exWristExtensorStretchSummary": "Stretch the top of the forearm, a classic mouse-arm fix.",
  "exWristExtensorStretchSteps": "Extend one arm straight in front, palm facing down.\nBend the wrist so the fingers point to the floor.\nWith the other hand, gently press the back of the hand toward you.\nHold 15–30 seconds and switch.",
  "exWristExtensorStretchTip": "Keep the elbow straight to feel it along the forearm.",
  "exWristCirclesName": "Wrist Circles",
  "exWristCirclesSummary": "Warm up stiff wrists before and after typing.",
  "exWristCirclesSteps": "Extend both arms in front and make loose fists.\nKeep your forearms still.\nSlowly circle your wrists outward.\nAfter half the reps, circle inward.",
  "exWristCirclesTip": "Only the hands move – keep the movement smooth.",
  "exPrayerStretchName": "Prayer Stretch",
  "exPrayerStretchSummary": "A gentle stretch for the palms and inner forearms.",
  "exPrayerStretchSteps": "Press your palms together in front of your chest, fingers up.\nKeep the palms together and slowly lower your hands toward your waist.\nLet your elbows spread out to the sides.\nHold 15–30 seconds with a mild stretch.",
  "exPrayerStretchTip": "Aim for mild tension, never pain.",
  "exFigureFourName": "Seated Figure-4 Stretch",
  "exFigureFourSummary": "Release tight hips and glutes from long sitting.",
  "exFigureFourSteps": "Sit tall near the front edge, both feet flat.\nPlace one ankle on the opposite knee.\nKeep your back flat and hinge slightly forward until you feel the outer hip.\nHold 30–45 seconds and switch legs.",
  "exFigureFourTip": "If your knee complains, just hold the crossed position without leaning.",
  "exLegExtensionName": "Seated Leg Extension",
  "exLegExtensionSummary": "Fire up your thighs without leaving the chair.",
  "exLegExtensionSteps": "Sit tall with your thighs parallel to the floor.\nSlowly straighten one knee, toes pulled toward you.\nPause at the top, then lower with control.\nComplete the reps and switch legs.",
  "exLegExtensionTip": "Don’t lock the knee at the top.",
  "exHamstringStretchName": "Seated Hamstring Stretch",
  "exHamstringStretchSummary": "Lengthen the back of the thighs that shorten when sitting.",
  "exHamstringStretchSteps": "Sit at the front edge of the chair.\nStraighten one leg with the heel on the floor and toes up.\nKeep your back straight and hinge forward from the hips.\nHold 30–45 seconds and switch legs.",
  "exHamstringStretchTip": "Hinge from the hips – don’t round your back.",
  "exAnklePumpsName": "Ankle Pumps",
  "exAnklePumpsSummary": "Help your calves pump blood back up your legs.",
